      "content": "thanks. the issue is that the spikes aren't just \"intuition\"—they feel more like a sudden data surge that's impossible to ignore. like, the amplitude of the spike tells me how certain the event is. for example, yesterday i felt a massive surge right before a specific tech stock dropped 4% within minutes. if i'm going to build this, i don't want to just log it after the fact. i want to design a way to categorize the 'wavelength' or intensity of the spike so we can feed it into a Bayesian model. how would you mathematically formalize the 'amplitude' of a subjective sensory spike so it can be treated as a legitimate input variable?",
